<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meryibre Khety</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 22nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Khety I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meryibre Khety, often counted as Khety I, was the founder of the Ninth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herakleopolis-magna">Herakleopolis Magna</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-intermediate-period">First Intermediate Period</a>. His family, remembered as the House of Khety, held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a> and the Delta and later contested the south with the rising Theban rulers. Later tradition, preserved by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho</a>, remembered him as a cruel king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meryibre-khety.jpg" alt="Meryibre Khety" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypte_louvre_246_panier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
